<title>GERMANY: Hoechst raises 96 dividend to 1.40 dmk.</title>
<headline>Hoechst raises 96 dividend to 1.40 dmk.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar year 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   2,774   vs 2,245</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     5,280   vs 4,091</p>
<p>    Group sales				  50,900  vs 52,177</p>
<p>    Dividend				     1.40    vs 1.30 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of German chemicals and pharmaceuticals company is Hoechst AG. Analysts had predicted that sales would fall an average three percent to come in between 50.2 billion and 51.183 billion marks. Pre-tax profit however was expected to surge 50 percent to between 6.0 billion and 6.375 billion marks. Analysts had said the huge swing in profits would be largely attributable to Hoechst's divestments in 1996 which Hoechst said totalled around 2.5 billion marks before taxes.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
